          "body": "Ireland's 20-17 win at the Aviva Stadium on Saturday rested on two first-half penalties they declined in favour of the corner, turned into tries for Rob Baloucoune and Rónan Kelleher. The Bok scrum still dominated, and Morné van den Berg's try plus five points from Sacha Feinberg-Mngomezulu kept the visitors in touch at the break. Malcolm Marx answered Sam Prendergast's penalty with a try, and the losing bonus point was enough to beat New Zealand to top spot in the south."
